    "page_name": "Citizen Workflow & Privacy Protections",
    "feature_name": "C0-Scope",
    "description": "Detailed instructions on citizen privacy, personal records retrieval, and grievance escalation.",
    "detailed_explanation": "As an authenticated citizen in AICM, your session is protected with privacy-by-design principles:\n- Personal records (survey plot, filed complaints) are strictly partitioned and inaccessible to other citizens.\n- When reporting grievances, you receive an anonymized alias (e.g. \"Citizen 042\") for public-facing reports.\n- Grievance tracking updates display official notes added by municipal engineers.\n- Building pre-checks against parcel 412/2 simulate real setback rules without recording private requests to public registries.",
